.TH ZVM-INSTALL 1 "August 2026" "ZVM" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-install \- download and install Zig and ZLS versions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm install
.RI [ options ]
.I version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download and install the requested Zig version.
Use
.B master
for the latest development build.
Version shorthand and aliases are accepted; see
.BR zvm (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --zls
Also install a ZLS release compatible with the resolved Zig version.
.TP
.BR -f , " " --force
Install even when the version is already present.
.TP
.BR -s , " " --skip-shasum
Skip SHA-256 verification and the confirmation normally required for an
unverified download.
This weakens download verification.
.TP
.BR -k , " " --skip-use
Install without setting the installed Zig version as active.
.TP
.BR --full
Use the full ZLS compatibility mode instead of the default runtime-only mode.
.TP
.BR --nomirror
Download Zig directly from ziglang.org instead of a community mirror.
.TP
.BR --target-os " " os
Override the target operating system.
This also sets
.B ZVM_TARGET_OS
for the operation.
.TP
.BR --target-arch " " architecture
Override the target architecture.
This also sets
.B ZVM_TARGET_ARCH
for the operation.
.TP
.BR --http.timeout " " seconds
Set the HTTP timeout for installation requests.
This also sets
.B ZVM_HTTP_TIMEOUT
for the operation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zvm install 0.14.1
zvm i .14
zvm install --zls --full master
zvm install --target-os freebsd --target-arch x86_64 0.14.1
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-use (1),
.BR zvm-list-remote (1),
.BR zvm-mirrorlist (1),
.BR zvm-vmu (1)
